{"id":8188723,"docketId":65286464,"caseName":"Kelliher v. Investment & Securities Co.","caseNameFull":"Kelliher v. Investment & Securities Co.","slug":"kelliher-v-investment-securities-co","docketNumber":"No. 286","dateFiled":"1934-10-08","dateArgued":null,"dateCertGranted":null,"year":1934,"scdbId":"","direction":"","votesMajority":null,"votesMinority":null,"disposition":"","posture":"","syllabus":null,"summary":null,"headnotes":null,"proceduralHistory":null,"attorneys":"Mr. M. M. Kelliher, Amy Kelliher, and Tena Marsh, pro se. Mr. Channing Wake-field for appellees.","natureOfSuit":"","citationCount":0,"judges":"","jurisdictionType":"","opinions":[{"id":8150654,"type":"majority","typeCode":"020lead","perCuriam":false,"author":"","joinedBy":"","pageCount":null,"textLength":2416,"isHtml":true,"text":"<opinion type=\"majority\">\n<author id=\"Aja\">\n<em>Per Curiam:</em>\n</author>\n<p id=\"ADO\">The motion of the appellees to dismiss the appeal herein is granted, and the appeal is <page-number citation-index=\"1\" label=\"520\">*520</page-number>dismissed (1) for the want of a substantial federal question <em>(Commercial Bank </em>v. <em>Buckingham\u2019s Executors, </em><span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"86424\"><a href=\"/opinion/86424/president-of-the-commercial-bank-of-cincinnati-v-buckinghams-executors/#342\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: President of the Commercial Bank of Cincinnati v....\">5 How. 317, 342, 343</a></span>; <em>Boss </em>v. <em>Oregon, </em><span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"97766\"><a href=\"/opinion/97766/ross-v-oregon/#161\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Ross v. Oregon\">227 U. S. 150, 161, 162</a></span>; <em>Quong Ham Wah Co. v. Industrial Commission, </em><span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"99758\"><a href=\"/opinion/99758/quong-ham-wah-co-v-industrial-accident-commn-of-cal/#448\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Quong Ham Wah Co. v. Industrial Accident Comm&#x27;n of Cal.\">255 U. S. 445, 448, 449</a></span>), and (2) for the want of a properly-presented federal question <em>(Live Oak Water Users Assn, v. Railroad Commission, </em><span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"100755\"><a href=\"/opinion/100755/live-oak-water-users-assn-v-railroad-commission/#357\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Live Oak Water Users&#x27; Ass&#x27;n v. Railroad Commission\">269 U. S. 354, 357, 358</a></span>; <em>Rooker v. Fidelity Trust Co., </em><span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"100125\"><a href=\"/opinion/100125/rooker-v-fidelity-trust-co/#117\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Rooker v. Fidelity Trust Co.\">261 U. S. 114, 117</a></span>; <em>Godchaux </em>v. <em>Estopinal, </em><span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"9418396\"><a href=\"/opinion/99484/godchaux-co-v-estopinal/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Godchaux Co. v. Estopinal\">251 U. S. 179</a></span>; <em>Archerd v. Oregon, </em><span class=\"citation\" data-id=\"8149725\"><a href=\"/opinion/8187794/archerd-v-oregon/\" aria-description=\"Citation for case: Archerd v. Oregon\">290 U. S. 604</a></span>). The motion for leave to proceed further herein <em>in forma pauperis </em>is denied.</p>\n<attorneys id=\"ABU\"><em>Mr. M. M. Kelliher, Amy Kelliher, </em>and <em>Tena Marsh, pro se. Mr. Channing Wake-field </em>for appellees.</attorneys>\n</opinion>"}],"citations":[]}